---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import {hrefFor,vaultInfo} from '@/lib/vault';
const snapshotDate = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB',{dateStyle:'long',timeZone:'Europe/Zurich'}).format(new Date(vaultInfo.importedAt));
---
<BaseLayout title="How to use the compendium">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">KEEP THE ANSWER CLOSE</p>
      <h1>How to use the compendium</h1>
      <p>A reference you can browse between sessions and reach for when it’s your turn.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="library-grid">
      <article class="note-card">
        <h2><a href="/search/">Find an answer</a></h2>
        <p>Ask a question or search names and phrases across the full reference text. Matching common questions show a short source-backed answer; section matches jump to the relevant heading. Narrow results by section. Open search with Ctrl+K on Windows or ⌘K on Mac.</p>
        <div class="related-links"><a href="/questions/">Browse common questions →</a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="note-card">
        <h2><a href="/level-up/">Check what changes at my level</a></h2>
        <p>Choose your subclass and class route. Keep character level and Wizard level distinct, then see spellbook acquisitions, baseline prepared spells, cantrips, spell slots, and the linked level-by-level guide.</p>
        <p>Copied spells and personal choices can increase or change your actual spellbook. The tool reports the printed route, not an imported character sheet.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="note-card">
        <h2><a href="/spells/">Choose a spell, item, or form</a></h2>
        <p>Use the spell, item, and form filters to build a shortlist. Select up to four entries and compare their recorded details side by side.</p>
        <p>Return from a reference with <em>Back to finder</em>, or use <em>Edit this shortlist</em> in a comparison, to keep your filters and selections.</p>
        <p>These are the vault’s selected entries and embedded creature galleries. Creature review status separates metadata-checked cards from image-transcribed references. Read conditional stats and the original image; gallery placement does not grant spell eligibility. A source label is not an access grant, and a checked candidate still needs the spell’s other requirements.</p>
        <div class="related-links"><a href="/items/">Magic items →</a><a href="/forms/">Creature forms →</a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="note-card">
        <h2><a href="/builds/">Follow a build</a></h2>
        <p>Choose a subclass and class structure in the build matrix, then open its level-by-level spell progression. All seven supported subclasses have equal space.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="note-card">
        <h2><a href="/tools/">Work out a number</a></h2>
        <p>Use the saving-throw, concentration, expected-damage, and component-cost calculators. Each tool explains its inputs, assumptions, and linked rules reference.</p>
        <p>Save a component plan in this browser and restore it later, or export/import a JSON backup. Unknown prices remain unknown. Importing a plan does not change the source spell rules or save anything automatically.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="note-card">
        <h2><a href="/tiers/">Read tables comfortably</a></h2>
        <p>Tables scroll horizontally when needed. Choose <em>Read rows</em> to see one entry at a time, with every field labelled. <em>Compare columns</em> restores the table.</p>
        <p>Tier colours help you scan; conditional ratings such as B/A retain their full labels. Open the reference for the conditions behind a rating.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="note-card">
        <h2><a href="/library/?saved=1">Keep a reading list</a></h2>
        <p>Choose <em>Save reference</em> on a page to keep it close. Open your reading list to revisit it, or choose the same control to remove it.</p>
        <p>The list stays in this browser on this device. It does not synchronize with Obsidian or another browser.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="note-card">
        <h2><a href="/play/">Use it at the table</a></h2>
        <p>Open the combat dashboard, reaction and concentration references, or the rules desk. Page contents preserve the vault’s edition notes and limits; ratings are advice, not additional rules.</p>
        <div class="related-links"><a href={hrefFor('Problem Navigator')}>Start with a problem →</a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="note-card">
        <h2><a href="/play/import/">Update your PDF sheet</a></h2>
        <p>Open your PDF, edit supported form fields, or cover a printed value and add replacement text. Save it in this browser and export an updated copy after your session.</p>
        <p>Your sheet stays on your device. Export backups: clearing browser data can remove saved sheets. A cover hides text visually; it does not securely erase the underlying text.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="note-card">
        <h2><a href="/library/">Browse the whole library</a></h2>
        <p>Explore the vault by topic. References retain their linked notes, images, callouts, and sources. Use <em>On this page</em> to jump to a heading, <em>Copy link</em> beside a heading to share the exact section, and <em>Print</em> for a paper reference.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <section class="guide-updates tool-panel" id="keeping-current" aria-labelledby="updates-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE PUBLISHED REFERENCE</p>
      <h2 id="updates-title">Keeping the compendium current</h2>
      <p>The website is a published copy of the Obsidian vault. The owner makes changes in Obsidian, imports the updated vault, checks the website, and publishes a new build. Changes in Obsidian appear here after that update is published.</p>
      <p class="snapshot-date">Latest vault snapshot: <time datetime={vaultInfo.importedAt}>{snapshotDate}</time>.</p>
      <p>On a reference page, open <em>Sources, edition &amp; updates</em> to see its note update date, website snapshot, and recorded review scope. An update date describes the content copy; it does not mean every rule was freshly checked.</p>
      <p>Your saved references and PDF sheets stay in this browser on this device. Export your PDF after a session to keep a portable copy.</p>
      <p class="calculator-note">The <a href={hrefFor('Vault Guide')}>original Obsidian vault guide</a> is preserved separately. Its editing commands, templates, and Obsidian settings apply to the vault.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
